# Base URL of a deployed AgentShield AWS Lambda API (from `sam deploy`'s
# ApiUrl output, minus the trailing slash), e.g.:
#   https://xxxxxxxxxx.execute-api.<region>.amazonaws.com/prod
#
# Optional. When unset, the "AWS Lambda (live)" option is hidden from the
# Live Demo system selector and the app behaves exactly as it does for
# local-only development -- this is the single place that URL is
# configured; nothing else in the frontend hardcodes it.
#
# This repo's own .env.development / .env.production commit the real
# invoke URL for the project's demo deployment -- that's fine to commit,
# since an API Gateway invoke URL carries no credentials or account ID,
# unlike an access key or secret. If you deploy your own stack, point
# these files (or a local .env.development.local / .env.production.local,
# which ARE gitignored) at your own ApiUrl instead.
VITE_AWS_API_BASE_URL=
